    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d82">

                <pb facs="0223" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4727/39 A.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Brazilian
                    Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic">January 20,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to confirm in writing what Mr. Hale,
                    at my request, stated to you orally, that the President will be pleased to place
                    his yacht, the <hi rendition="#italic">Mayflower</hi>, at your disposal on the
                    afternoon of Monday, <pb facs="0224" n="112" xml:id="pg112"/> February 14, to
                    convey the remains of the late Ambassador Nabuco from Washington to Hampton
                    Roads, where the remains will be transferred to the cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Montana</hi>, which will convey them, escorted by
                    yourself, to Rio de Janeiro.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
